=== Using Arrays as Sets ===

Auto-creating array elements by access:
  After x[1]:
    1 in x: 1
    2 in x: 0
    x[1]: 
    x[2]: 

Initial set:
  apple
  banana
  cherry

Membership tests:
  apple is in the set
  grape is NOT in the set

Adding 'grape' to set (traditional: set["grape"] = 1)
  grape is now in the set

Adding 'mango' to set (just by accessing: set["mango"])
  mango is now in the set

Removing 'banana' from set
  banana is NOT in the set (removed)

Toggle operations:
  Removing cherry
  Adding orange

Final set:
  apple
  grape
  mango
  orange

=== Set Operations ===
Set1:  ["a", "b", "c"]
Set2:  ["b", "c", "d"]
Union:  ["a", "b", "c", "d"]
Intersection:  ["b", "c"]
Difference:  ["a"]
